# 21. AI should have three execution tiers

The canonical AI architecture should be:

```text
             REQUEST
                │
      ┌─────────┼─────────┐
      │         │         │
      ▼         ▼         ▼
 deterministic browser   remote
      core        AI       AI
```

### Tier 0 — no AI

Always ask first:

> Can deterministic code solve this?

For domain combinations:

yes.

Do that immediately.

### Tier 1 — local browser AI

Good for:

* embeddings
* semantic matching
* reranking
* classification
* tiny models
* privacy-sensitive inference

Transformers.js currently supports GPU inference through WebGPU via ONNX Runtime. ([Hugging Face][16])

Benefits:

```text
0 network latency
0 inference bill
privacy
offline capability
user supplies compute
```

But only use it when the model download/startup cost makes sense.

Downloading a 500 MB model to save a 200 ms request is obviously counterproductive.

