# 25. Browser-agent optimization is its own layer

An agent may reach your product without MCP.

Maybe it only has a browser.

Your website should therefore be unusually easy for machines to operate.

Use actual:

```html
<nav>
<main>
<article>
<form>
<label>
<input>
<button>
<table>
```

rather than:

```html
<div class="thing">
<div onclick="...">
```

MDN emphasizes that semantic HTML exposes meaning in machine-readable form, not merely visually, and native controls carry useful semantics automatically. ([MDN Web Docs][19])

That helps:

