Core product information should exist in initial HTML whenever possible.

Google's current crawler documentation is an instructive example: rendering occurs later through a JavaScript rendering system, and Google explicitly recommends keeping important HTML lean and placing essential metadata/content where it can reliably be fetched. ([Google for Developers][20])

For agents this matters even more.

A browser agent shouldn't have to:

```text
