# 27. Give every important page a clean machine-readable equivalent

There is now a useful emerging convention here.

`llms.txt` remains a **proposal rather than a formal web standard**, but its August 2026 v2 revision reflects substantial real-world adoption and adds discovery using link relations for markdown equivalents. ([llms-txt][21])

I would implement:

```text
/llms.txt
```

plus clean Markdown versions of important documentation.

And where useful:

```html
<link
  rel="alternate"
  type="text/markdown"
  href="/docs/api.md">
```

The MCP documentation itself now prominently exposes its docs through `llms.txt` and markdown representations, which is a useful signal about where agent-oriented technical documentation is heading. ([Model Context Protocol][22])

But don't confuse this with MCP.

`llms.txt` helps agents **read** the website.

MCP lets them **operate** the product.

