# 29. OAuth for MCP should follow the actual MCP architecture

Protected remote MCP servers shouldn't invent auth.

MCP currently uses OAuth-based protected-resource discovery, including RFC 9728 metadata and resource indicators, so clients can discover authorization infrastructure instead of needing custom setup. ([Model Context Protocol][23])

This matters because an agent should ideally be able to go from:

```text
MCP server URL
```

to:

```text
discover auth
authorize
call tool
```

without reading your documentation manually.

That is agent UX.

