# 33. The canonical optimization hierarchy

When an agent wants to make something faster, it should optimize in this order:

```text
1. Eliminate work
2. Eliminate network round trips
3. Eliminate model calls
4. Batch operations
5. Parallelize independent operations
6. Cache stable results
7. Move computation nearer its data
8. Stream partial results
9. Reduce payload/token size
10. Move CPU work off main thread
11. Profile algorithms
12. Choose faster runtime
13. Choose faster language
14. Micro-optimize code
```

This is a key point.

**Rust is #13, not #1.**

