```

Results:

```text
available .com #1 appears
```

potentially before the AI call is even finished.

Agent interface:

```text
search_domains(
  description="AI agent news site",
  liked_names=["AgentSpy","AgentWatch"],
  tlds=["com"],
  search_depth=1000,
  result_limit=20
)
```

One MCP call.

REST:

```text
POST /v1/domains/search
```

same operation.

Bulk automation:

```text
POST /v1/domains/search
Accept: application/x-ndjson
```

streams potentially thousands of results.

The website and agent interfaces are therefore **different projections over one engine**.

That's what I would consider the correct architecture.

